# Token discipline

Spec: `docs/design/design-system.md` §3. It wins over anything here if the two
ever disagree.

## The rule

Every colour, font size, radius and container width comes from a token. If you
are about to type a hex, an `hsl(...)` literal, a `font-size` in pixels or a
`border-radius` in pixels, stop — find the token or add one to `global.css`.

This repo got audited and found **54 hardcoded hex colours** and **19 literal
font sizes**. Do not add the 55th.

## Colour

Base is neutral greyscale plus one brand accent, `--primary`. Figures use the
semantic data palette (`--data-new`, `--data-inert`, `--data-write`,
`--data-gain`, `--data-loss`). One accent means one thing.

**Dark mode is class-based and the shadcn tokens flip on their own.** Do not
write `dark:` pairs for foreground, background or muted — use `text-foreground`,
`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground` and let the token do it. A `dark:` pair
is correct only for opacity variants and for `dark:prose-invert`.

The `--color-legacy-*` crimson tokens are **out of bounds** here. They belong to
the WIP landing and to `about`, `contact` and `work`. Never introduce one into
notes, series, nav, footer or the CV.

## Type

Use the scale: `--text-display`, `--text-title`, `--text-subtitle`,
`--text-body`, `--text-ui`, `--text-meta`, `--text-micro`.

**11px is the floor.** No size below it, no half-pixel sizes. If a label does not
fit at 11px, drop the label — do not shrink it.

## Radius and width

Four radii: `sm` 6px, `md` 10px, `lg` 14px, `pill` 999px. Nothing else.

One page width: `--width-shell` (800px) for nav, footer and listings. Note prose
sits in `--measure` (66ch); figures may bleed to `--width-bleed` (880px). The CV
uses the shell width, same as everything else.

## Focus

Interactive elements need a visible focus ring. The global `:focus-visible` rule
covers links, buttons, inputs and `summary`. Do not set `outline: none` without
putting something back.
